// ADDRESS into the linear heap (the emitted code does
// `mem.u32(environ + i * 4)`), and 0 is used here as an empty, NULL-terminated
// block. That relies on address 0 reading as zero — the reserved null page,
// which no allocator hands out. If that ever stops holding, `getEnvVarsC`'s
// `while gEnv[i] != nil` walk reads garbage instead of terminating, and the
// symptom is a junk environment rather than a crash. Nothing else in this file
// depends on the heap.
