// strtod — the SAME SHAPE OF BUG AS `environ`, found the same way.
//
// `std/parseutils.parseFloat` has a fast path in Nim and a slow path that hands
// a NUL-terminated buffer to C's `strtod`. nimony-web's runtime.js does not
// provide one, so every bundle died with
//
//     ReferenceError: strtod is not defined
//         at parseBiggestFloat -> decodeFloat -> rawNext (nifreader)
//
// — and note WHERE: `decodeFloat` is in the NIF READER. This is not "aowli gets
// a float wrong", it is aowli failing to PARSE any `.s.nif` containing a float
// literal whose text misses the fast path. All four bundles, dead at the first
// such token, exit 1 with no output. Nothing noticed because the only fixture
// this lane ever ran was `echo "hello"; echo 42`.
